text:
The United Nations Park is located in the Bagmati Corridor, which is part of Lalitpur and next to the bagmati river Kathmandu District.  In this park, there are very big trees and plants which have made the environment very beautiful and green. Here, there is a place to do meditation yoga in the morning and various sports like volleyball, badminton.  Different films and videos are shot here at different times.  There is no fee to enter this park.  There is a lot of people here in the morning.  Nowadays, with the increase in the movement of people, various dirty plastics have been thrown here and there, which has made the environment of the UN Park turbulent, we all citizens are conscious.  So it is our responsibility not to litter here, dustbins are also kept here.
Some current problems in this Park;
Due to incessant rains between September 26 and 28, the mouth of the Bagmati river rose and flooded.  Flood had created a huge disaster in Kathmandu Lalitpur and damaged all the small houses and roads on the banks of the river.  Similarly, in this UN Park, the mouth of the Bagmati River has risen and damaged the entire structure inside the UN Park. .  The bridge connecting Dhobikhola Basant Marg located in Kathmandu from UN Park has been swept away by the flood and the complete construction of the bridge itself is necessary. It seems necessary for the concerned body to complete it. The walls of the park are broken, plants have been damaged and all the paths have been damaged. As a result, the greenery of the UN Park is covered with dirt.  Ihope that the structures here will be the same as before and the greenery will be as before.
